pokebw2-hwaddr.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): DS hardware addresses that pokebw2 writes as numbers
where Black's C uses the SDK's names. On the PC libntr's HW_ names are the host's copies of VRAM and palette RAM; the
number is an unmapped address (each crashed at it, or would). As Black's files:
- the opening event's VRAM clear (src/ov035/event_mapchange.c, ClearLCDCVram: NEW GAME after the professor's intro):
  HW_LCDC_VRAM, HW_LCDC_VRAM_SIZE (Black's src/ov020/event_mapchange.c);
- the building-entry fade's bank D clear (src/ov036/field_transition.c, EventGameTransition_RunDefaultFadeIn: the
  first walk into Aspertia's north): HW_LCDC_VRAM (Black's src/ov021/field_transition.c);
- the field effect's capture dimming (src/ov036/fld3d_ci.c, EventFieldEffect_DimCaptureColor): HW_LCDC_VRAM_D (Black's
  src/ov021/fld3d_ci.c);
- the C-Gear help's palette write (src/ov200/cg_help.c, 0x050005e2): HW_DB_BG_PLTT + 0x1e2 (the sub screen's BG
  palette, color 0xf1).
The DS build's code is the same.

diff --git a/src/ov035/event_mapchange.c b/src/ov035/event_mapchange.c
